  "brief": "We run a community bike-share scheme. At the moment we have 1,400 registered riders. Counting sign-ups and people leaving, we are gaining a net 30 riders every month. Our depot can service at most 1,900 riders without breaking its maintenance targets, and the council wants us to stay under that ceiling, without turning anyone away, over the next ten months. We could rent a second depot for £2,400 a month, starting in month 3, which would lift the ceiling by about 600 riders, or add a Sunday maintenance crew for £700 a month, which would lift it by about 150. We could also carry on as we are. Our grant limits extra spending to £3,000 a month, and we cannot recruit more than one extra person. I'd like to know which choice keeps us under the ceiling.",
  "scenario_created_at": "2026-10-10T00:35:48.393294+00:00"
}
